1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Why do two 20 million dong transfers chime identically in three seconds, but one moves zero reserve money while the other moves billions across accounts at the central bank?

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,100
An intra-bank On-Us transfer never leaves the commercial bank building.

3
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:23,000
The core banking server merely updates two customer lines in its database, keeping one hundred percent of its low-cost CASA deposit pool.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,780
An inter-bank Off-Us transfer cannot edit another bank's ledger.

5
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:36,000
In three seconds, the national switch validates the sending bank's collateral quota and guarantees instant credit to the recipient under central-bank rules.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,210
Behind the scenes, commercial banks do not shuttle tiny amounts back and forth all day.

7
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:50,000
At clearing cut-off, the switch nets 500 billion in outbound orders against 470 billion in inbound orders into a single 30 billion transfer at the central bank, saving 940 billion in intraday liquidity.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:01,000
High-value wholesale orders of ten billion or more route through the central bank's RTGS expressway, while year-end delayed transfers must be parked in Account 113 as cash in transit.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:09,420
That three-second chime is either a simple internal database edit or an engineering masterpiece of national clearing collateral and multilateral net settlement.

10
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,000
That is the hidden journey of where money sleeps.
